WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.009
This short guide shows ISSV students and parents how to join a virtual Sunday class.

00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:14.267
First, make sure you’re signed in with your ISSV school account, not a parent’s or personal Gmail.

00:00:14.417 --> 00:00:20.221
On a shared computer, add a separate Chrome profile just for school, and use it every time.

00:00:20.821 --> 00:00:27.414
Next, go to classroom.google.com, or open the Classroom app. Your class is already there.

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:29.997
If you see a Join button on it, click it.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:37.180
On a virtual Sunday, open your class and click Join next to Meet. It’s the same link every week.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:43.200
Before you join, turn your microphone off and keep your camera on. Then click Join now.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.440
In class, keep your camera on, and stay muted until it’s your turn to speak.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.237
To ask a question, click Raise hand.

00:00:52.387 --> 00:00:59.129
Join by 10:15 to test your sound. Class runs until 1:30, just like a normal Sunday.

00:00:59.729 --> 00:01:03.869
If you’re stuck on Asking to join, you’re probably on the wrong account.

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:09.525
Click your profile picture, switch to your school account, and open the link again from Classroom.

00:01:10.125 --> 00:01:17.443
That’s it! The written steps are on the Online Classes page of the school website. Still stuck? Email the school office.
